      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The lake’s inlet and outlet both emerge from the same end, a rare hydrological feature noted by early settlers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_Lake%2C_Wyoming_County%2C_New_York",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Silver Lake’s name comes from an Indigenous term meaning “large flats,” long before the western state of Wyoming rose to prominence.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.scientificmagz.blog/silver-lake-wyoming-county-guide",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The historic Silver Lake Institute, listed on the National Register in 1985, sits on the east bank and reflects the town’s 19th‑century religious heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_Lake%2C_Wyoming_County%2C_New_York",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "An annual Pioneer Picnic has marked the first Sunday in August since 1874, drawing families to the lake’s historic grounds.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_Lake%2C_Wyoming_County%2C_New_York",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Silver Lake’s shallow, temperate waters have made it a longtime favorite for fishing, boating, and family recreation in Western New York.",
